# Windows batch files are run by cmd.exe, which is unreliable with LF-only
# line endings. Store them byte-for-byte with the CRLF endings they already
# have, and never convert them.
#
# "-text" (no conversion at all) rather than "text eol=crlf" on purpose:
# "text" normalises to LF *in the repository*, and raw.githubusercontent.com
# serves the stored blob unconverted - so anyone downloading install.bat from
# a raw link would get an LF-only file back. "-text" keeps CRLF in the blob,
# so clones, ZIP archives and raw downloads all produce a working file.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text
